=== Prompt ===
Who is Gandalf?

=== Response ===
Gandalf is a prominent character from J.R.R. Tolkien's "The Lord of the Rings" series and other works in his legendarium. He is a Maia, a type of powerful spirit in Tolkien's mythology, who took on a wizard's form. Gandalf is one of the Istari, a group of wizards sent to Middle-earth to aid against the growing darkness.

In the narrative, Gandalf is depicted as a tall, bearded figure with flowing robes, often seen wielding a staff. He plays a crucial role in guiding and supporting the hobbits Frodo Baggins and company in their quest to destroy the One Ring. Throughout the series, Gandalf demonstrates great wisdom, courage, and magical power, often appearing at key moments to provide guidance or assistance when it is most needed.

His character evolves significantly over the course of the story, particularly in "The Two Towers," where he faces a dramatic transformation after being captured and seemingly killed by the Balrog. He returns in "The Return of the King" as a wiser and more powerful being, known as Gandalf the White.

Gandalf is celebrated for his deep understanding of the world and its history, his unwavering dedication to justice and the fight against evil, and his ability to inspire others through his actions and words.

